What will determine the outlook to 2034?
The next decisive indicators are whether announced expansions enter qualified production, whether new process nodes achieve acceptable yields and whether customers secure capacity beyond a single geography. Mature-node capacity will remain important wherever cost, reliability and application-specific functions outrank maximum transistor density. Specialty foundries may therefore grow through differentiation even if leading-edge process announcements dominate industry headlines.

The reported market forecast is a scenario for the contracted fabrication economy, not a promise that every announced project or node will reach commercial scale. Tracking customer qualification, utilization, actual wafer shipments and process-specific pricing will provide a firmer view of opportunity than counting construction announcements alone.

